  Reading notes (each makes the Go regexp at least as strict as upstream, so a
  value that passes it also passes Pi-hole):
  - ValidateDomain lowercases its input first (list.sh:102, domain="${1,,}");
    Nexus admits only lowercase values, so the regexes are used as written.
  - list.sh:111/112 are PCRE (grep -P) in bash double quotes, so "\\d" and "\\."
    reach grep as "\d" and "\."; RE2 reads both the same way.
  - list.sh:267 is a bash [[ =~ ]] ERE. Go reads the escaped "\#", "\." and
    "\ " in the bracket as "#", "." and " ". If bash also passes a literal "\"
    into the bracket, upstream accepts "\" as well: the Go form is then
    stricter, which is the safe direction for TC-6.
  - webpage.sh:542's ")-;" is a range (0x29-0x3B) in both ERE and RE2, so
    upstream CheckUrl accepts "*", "+", "," and ";" through it.
  - webpage.sh:546 strips the first "<scheme>://<userinfo>@" before the
    character check; URLPattern admits no "@", so that step never applies.
